# Stream Processing Models
#
# Batch, micro-batch, streaming dataflow, logs, and actors compared on windows, watermarks, backpressure, and recovery, then mapped onto a live chat torrent.

#>computing_stream_models
#:layer #!reference
#:domain #!computing
#:form #!comparison
#:level #!advanced
#:review #!adversarial_checked
#:valence #!bone

^"emit"{
 ~#title: "Stream Processing Models"
 ~#claim: "Stream systems differ in how they cut time into windows, decide when data is late, push back on fast producers, and recover state after a crash."
 ~#proof: "MapReduce, D-Streams, MillWheel, the Dataflow model, Flink snapshots, Kafka, and the actor papers each define one row."
 ~#door: "Read the matrix, then the watermark frame, then window a pile of chat cards by hand."
 ~#audience: "engineers building live pipelines, including chat tools for streamers"
 continuity: "Stream Processing Models | when data is late"
 cold_open: "A stream system is defined by how it decides when data is late, and by what it does with the stragglers."
}

